### Items Not Published in the Sourced Documents

The following requested line items were checked across all five documents but **no value was disclosed**, so they have been omitted from the table above rather than estimated:

- **Retail health GWP** — Annexure-II provides only segment splits by Health/PA/Travel, not Retail vs. Group GWP.
- **Claims ratio (IGAAP & IFRS)** — not published as a standalone computed ratio in either basis; only absolute incurred claims and premium components are disclosed.
- **Expense ratio (IGAAP)** — not disclosed as a metric distinct from the EoM ratio.
- **Commission ratio (IGAAP)** — only the absolute commission & brokerage (net) figure is disclosed, not a ratio.
- **Combined ratio (IGAAP)** — not disclosed anywhere in the Outcome of Financial Results or its ratio schedules.
- **Solvency ratio** — Note 5a confirms solvency is computed as of period-end, but no numeric value is shown in the disclosed tables.
- **Retail health market share** — not disclosed in any of the five sourced documents, including the Investor Relations index page.

## Key Observations

### PAT Divergence Between GAAP Bases
The 9MFY26 IGAAP result shows a **loss of ₹214.35 Cr**, while the IFRS result shows a **profit of ₹208.31 Cr** — a swing of over ₹420 Cr attributable purely to GAAP differences. This is driven primarily by IFRS 17 insurance contract measurement principles versus IGAAP revenue account treatment, compounded by differing treatment of the EoM excess-expense transfer across the two bases.

### Expense of Management Ceiling Breach
The company's **EoM ratio of 36.33%** for 9MFY26 continues to exceed the IRDAI-permitted ceiling of **35.90%** (inclusive of additional allowances). IRDAI forbearance on this breach appears to remain pending as of the filing date — a recurring regulatory overhang that has been flagged since FY24-25.

### Net Worth Trend
Net worth declined sequentially from **₹2,955.96 Cr** (as at September 2025) to **₹2,871.42 Cr** (as at December 2025), reflecting absorption of the cumulative IGAAP loss during the period.

### Growth Trajectory
The Regulation 52(4) schedule indicates Gross Direct Premium growth of **21.84%** for 9MFY26 cumulative, broadly flat versus **21.71%** in 9MFY25. However, the standalone December 2025 quarter shows a sharp acceleration to **54.73%** quarter-on-quarter growth, following a much weaker Q2 (**3.70%**) — suggesting a strong pickup in new business momentum in Q3 FY26 after a soft second quarter.</ans>
